WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.771
ALEX: What else changed besides the
price?

00:00:01.856 --> 00:00:06.499
JAMIE: Zero data retention by default
through the API. And there are what

00:00:06.499 --> 00:00:11.141
JAMIE: Anthropic calls preserved-
thinking anti-distillation protections —
that applies to API accounts created

00:00:11.141 --> 00:00:15.784
JAMIE: on or after August thirty-first.
Which means competitors can't as easily
train

00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:20.427
JAMIE: on Opus 5.5's reasoning traces.

00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:25.269
RUFUS: That's the interesting bit. The
zero retention and the anti-distillation
protections aren't

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:30.002
RUFUS: really a customer benefit.
They're a moat. Anthropic is saying: you
can

00:00:30.002 --> 00:00:34.734
RUFUS: use the outputs, but you cannot
reverse-engineer how it got there.
